# Line-ending policy, added 2026-09-08.
#
# Windows tools (PowerShell Set-Content, Python Path.write_text with the
# default newline=None) rewrite files with CRLF. Git stores LF. Without
# this file every such write shows as a full-file diff, and a real change
# hides inside it.
#
# "text=auto" means git stores LF and checks out native (CRLF here), so a
# CRLF working tree is CLEAN - which is what we want on Windows.
* text=auto

# Byte-stable types: never convert. Booksmith derives source_sha256 from
# sha256_file(source/source.html), a byte hash, so any EOL conversion
# there would silently change a release identity.
*.html    -text
*.pdf     -text
*.png     -text
*.jpg     -text
*.jpeg    -text
*.gif     -text
*.ttf     -text
*.otf     -text
*.woff    -text
*.woff2   -text
*.zip     -text
*.db      -text
*.sqlite3 -text
